! version = 2.0

+ (hi|hey|hello|howdy|yo|good morning|good afternoon|good evening)
* <get name> != undefined => {@ ctrlintent greet}{random}Hey <get name>!|Hello <get name>!|Good to see you, <get name>!{/random}
* <get currentSession> == development => {@ ctrlintent greet}Hey! Feel free to keep asking about Wilson's CV.
* <get currentSession> == closing => {@ ctrlintent greet}Hey! Feel free to keep asking about Wilson's CV.
* <get ctrl_greet> >= 1 => {@ ctrlintent greet}{random}Hey again!|Still here!{/random} You can tell me your name, or just ask about Wilson's CV.
- {@ ctrlintent greet}<set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=askname><set botIntention=<bot intent_askname>>{random}Hey!|Hello!|Hi there!{/random} What should I call you?

+ (my name is|it is|i am|im|you can call me|call me) *
* <get name> == <formal> => <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=givename><set botIntention=<bot intent_givename>>We already know each other, <get name>! How can I help today?
- <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=givename><set botIntention=<bot intent_givename>>Nice to meet you, {formal}<star2>{/formal}.<set name={formal}<star2>{/formal}> How can I help you today?

// % (Previous) block: catches a BARE name reply — just "Ana", no "my name
// is" prefix — that the trigger above can't, since it requires one of
// those lead-in phrases. Scoped to the bot's last line asking for a name
// (either phrasing: the initial ask or the repeat-greeting nudge), so it
// only activates in that exact context — RiveScript checks % matches
// before any normal trigger, so an unscoped version of this would
// swallow any single-word message (confirmed by testing: it captured
// "skills" as if it were a name). Rather than exclude every existing
// single-word CV trigger (fragile, needs updating every time one's
// added), it asks for confirmation instead — safe regardless of whether
// the word happens to collide with real vocabulary.
//
// [*] not *, on both sides: * requires 1+ trailing characters, but "...
// what should i call you" has nothing after it once the "?" is stripped
// — a bare * there never matches (confirmed by testing: it silently
// fell through to the generic fallback). [*] allows zero-width, so it
// still matches when there's nothing left to consume.
//
// Greeting words are excluded and redirected back to the real trigger
// (<get ctrl_greet> already handles a repeat "hi" with its own nudge) —
// otherwise a second "hi" gets treated as a candidate name instead of a
// greeting (confirmed by testing: "Is Hi your name?").
+ _
% [*] (what should i call you|you can tell me your name) [*]
* <star> == hi => {@ <star>}
* <star> == hey => {@ <star>}
* <star> == hello => {@ <star>}
* <star> == howdy => {@ <star>}
* <star> == yo => {@ <star>}
- <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=confirmname><set botIntention=<bot intent_confirmname>><set pendingname={formal}<star>{/formal}>Is <get pendingname> your name?

// {formal} is regex-processed before <set>/<get> tags resolve, so
// {formal}<get pendingname>{/formal} would format the literal text
// "<get pendingname>" instead of its value (confirmed by testing — it
// printed "undefined"). <star> is safe inside {formal} because it's
// substituted earlier, before {formal} runs — so pendingname is
// formatted once at capture time above, then reused plain below.
+ (yes|yeah|yep|correct|thats right|that is right|right)
% is * your name
- <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=givename><set botIntention=<bot intent_givename>>Nice to meet you, <get pendingname>.<set name=<get pendingname>> How can I help you today?

+ (no|nope|not quite|thats not right|that is not right|wrong)
% is * your name
- <set unknownStreak=0><set userIntention=askname><set botIntention=<bot intent_askname>>Got it. Please tell me your name like this: "My name is Ana".

+ (what is my name|do you know my name|remember my name)
* <get name> != undefined => You told me your name is <get name>.
- I do not know it yet. You can say "my name is Ana".

+ (who are you|what are you|what is your name|your name|tell me about yourself)
